Subject: [PATCH 7/8 RFC] dt-bindings: media: make amlogic,ao-sysctrl optional

A decoder attached to a power domain does not program the AO sleep and
isolation bits itself, so the sysctrl phandle is not needed. Keep it
required for every compatible that has no power domain, so GX, G12 and SM1
nodes still have to describe where the AO registers live.

---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml
index 631ba0a..18c9488 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml
@@ -86,6 +86,12 @@ properties:
     description: should point to a canvas provider node
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
 
+  power-domains:
+    description:
+      Power domain owning the AO sleep and isolation bits of the decoder.
+      When present the driver does not write amlogic,ao-sysctrl itself.
+    maxItems: 1
+
 allOf:
   - if:
       properties:
@@ -130,6 +136,16 @@ allOf:
         clock-names:
           minItems: 5
 
+  # Platforms without a power domain keep programming the AO registers, so the
+  # AO sysctrl stays mandatory for them.
+  - if:
+      not:
+        required:
+          - power-domains
+    then:
+      required:
+        - amlogic,ao-sysctrl
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
@@ -140,7 +156,6 @@ required:
   - clock-names
   - resets
   - reset-names
-  - amlogic,ao-sysctrl
   - amlogic,canvas
 
 additionalProperties: false
